WEBVTT

00:01.270 --> 00:03.390
So what do we do?

00:03.390 --> 00:06.420
You need to pass an exam to raise your rank.

00:06.420 --> 00:09.070
And before that, you need to prove yourself.

00:09.070 --> 00:13.660
And so you'll need to take jobs yourself.

00:14.880 --> 00:19.750
But if they know Rentt Faina is 
back in town, the guild will...

00:20.820 --> 00:25.410
Rentt, why not register as an 
adventurer under another name?

00:25.410 --> 00:29.220
I can't do that! Using two different 
names is against the guild rules!

00:29.220 --> 00:31.870
They'll never know.

00:31.870 --> 00:34.980
And even if they do find out, 
it won't be a big deal.

00:35.260 --> 00:37.840
Everyone knows Rentt Faina, and they'd have

00:37.840 --> 00:40.920
no end of questions about 
how you ended up that way.

00:41.240 --> 00:45.390
But nobody will ask questions 
about a wandering adventurer,

00:45.390 --> 00:48.050
no matter how strange they look.

00:48.510 --> 00:50.010
True.

00:50.010 --> 00:53.850
Well, you'll lose what 
accomplishments Rentt Faina had,

00:53.850 --> 00:58.850
and you'll have to start over from Iron.

00:59.200 --> 01:00.470
I don't mind.

01:01.010 --> 01:02.700
My goal is...

01:03.110 --> 01:06.970
to become a Mythril-class 
adventurer someday. That's all.

02:39.050 --> 02:43.180
<b> Bronze-class
Exam</b>

02:40.150 --> 02:44.180
You already defeated three orcs?

02:44.180 --> 02:45.110
Yes.

02:45.110 --> 02:46.390
Confirm, please.

02:47.180 --> 02:52.520
<i>For a solo adventurer like me, 
a magic bag is a necessity.</i>

02:53.060 --> 02:56.130
<i>It took me five years to save up the 
money for it, but it was worth it.</i>

02:57.450 --> 03:01.390
They've been dressed properly 
and are well-preserved.

03:01.960 --> 03:04.720
I'm sure the client will be satisfied.

03:05.190 --> 03:07.490
So the job's complete, yes?

03:07.490 --> 03:08.380
Yes.

03:09.790 --> 03:10.860
What is it?

03:11.330 --> 03:14.300
Um, can you wait a moment?

03:14.900 --> 03:16.270
That's fine, but...

03:18.890 --> 03:20.310
Hey, did you hear?

03:20.310 --> 03:21.930
He took down three orcs.

03:22.320 --> 03:24.060
Who is that guy?

03:24.060 --> 03:25.620
I've never seen him around here.

03:26.550 --> 03:30.300
<i>I guess as a rookie Iron-class, 
I stood out too much.</i>

03:30.300 --> 03:31.760
Here you go.

03:33.560 --> 03:34.690
What's this?

03:34.950 --> 03:37.050
I just spoke to my manager.

03:37.400 --> 03:41.000
Rentt, why don't you try 
taking the promotion exam?

03:41.000 --> 03:42.450
Promotion exam?

03:42.450 --> 03:46.220
Yes, the promotion exam for Bronze-class.

03:46.220 --> 03:49.370
It's rare for somebody to get the 
opportunity so soon after registering,

03:49.370 --> 03:51.780
but you seem to have the potential.

03:54.020 --> 03:56.060
I'd love to.

03:57.740 --> 04:00.540
So, you've already been asked to 
take the promotion exam for Bronze?

04:00.930 --> 04:04.810
Well, it makes sense, with your ability.

04:04.810 --> 04:07.310
It's partially thanks to this body.

04:07.310 --> 04:10.010
Yes, but that just means you're 
capable of using its strength.

04:10.010 --> 04:14.390
So, what name did you register 
under at the guild?

04:15.650 --> 04:17.160
Rentt Vivie.

04:21.820 --> 04:23.030
You okay?

04:24.490 --> 04:26.860
No, not really.

04:27.580 --> 04:29.980
Why Vivie?

04:29.980 --> 04:33.140
If you use my family name when 
everyone knows I was close to you,

04:33.140 --> 04:34.580
people will be suspicious!

04:34.900 --> 04:38.790
It wouldn't be fair to you to have 
people thinking you had a weird man

04:38.790 --> 04:40.560
coming and going from your home.

04:41.380 --> 04:44.000
So I decided I'd be your relative.

04:45.290 --> 04:49.190
Well, I guess I can understand that...

04:49.190 --> 04:53.650
But you don't need to worry 
about my reputation.

04:55.200 --> 04:59.670
I'm just a broke academic who came here 
'cause she couldn't make it in the capital.

04:59.670 --> 05:02.400
I don't care what people think about me.

05:03.730 --> 05:06.510
You've done a lot for me.

05:06.510 --> 05:09.210
I don't want to cause trouble for you.

05:09.210 --> 05:10.530
You've done a lot for me, too.

05:10.900 --> 05:15.990
The cooking, washing, cleaning... 
you do almost all of it.

05:15.990 --> 05:19.240
I owe you more than you owe me.

05:19.620 --> 05:21.370
That's not true.

05:22.010 --> 05:26.770
I'm still human because of you.

05:27.760 --> 05:28.900
Rentt...

05:30.350 --> 05:33.920
Then you can just stay 
here as long as you like.

05:33.920 --> 05:37.100
You're my relative, aren't you?

05:37.420 --> 05:39.930
Nothing wrong with imposing on family.

05:40.140 --> 05:41.290
Yeah?

05:41.930 --> 05:44.560
I'll take you up on that, then.

05:53.330 --> 05:55.370
Um, who are you?

05:55.850 --> 05:59.540
I'm Rentt Vivie. I'm here for the exam.

05:59.540 --> 06:01.380
Oh, you're him?

06:01.380 --> 06:04.970
Huh? Rentt? I didn't think 
you'd be coming today...

06:05.770 --> 06:08.100
I got approved to take the exam.

06:08.100 --> 06:12.970
Yes, but I assumed you'd wait for the 
next one so you had time to study.

06:12.970 --> 06:15.620
The next one is several months from now.

06:15.620 --> 06:16.720
But...

06:17.640 --> 06:21.050
Whew, I made it!

06:21.050 --> 06:23.300
<i>He'll lose points for that.</i>

06:23.300 --> 06:26.700
<i>An adventurer who can't show 
up on time isn't trustworthy.</i>

06:27.630 --> 06:30.390
Okay, Iron-class adventurers!

06:30.390 --> 06:33.660
We're about to begin the Bronze-class exam!

06:33.980 --> 06:35.790
First, the knowledge test!

06:35.790 --> 06:39.210
We'll test you on guild rules and the 
proper handling of monster drops.

06:39.210 --> 06:43.810
You'll have to prove you're 
ready to be Bronze-class.

06:44.340 --> 06:48.250
Only those who pass this exam will be 
allowed to take the practical portion.

06:48.510 --> 06:50.970
<i>The practical changes each time.</i>

06:51.460 --> 06:54.220
<i>When I did it, it was gathering herbs.</i>

06:54.220 --> 06:57.980
All right, anyone who's taking the 
written exam, come with me.

07:02.560 --> 07:04.170
Good luck!

07:04.170 --> 07:04.900
Thanks.

07:14.620 --> 07:16.580
<i>There are more people here than I thought.</i>

07:20.630 --> 07:22.280
<i>Isn't that girl...</i>

07:25.000 --> 07:25.830
Laura!

07:25.830 --> 07:26.610
Right!

07:31.910 --> 07:34.540
<i>I suppose her partner's taking the oral exam.</i>

07:35.780 --> 07:38.550
<i>It's rare for normal people 
to be able to read and write.</i>

07:39.140 --> 07:43.190
<i>I learned a lot of things in my village 
growing up, like reading, writing,</i>

07:43.190 --> 07:45.200
<i>and knowledge of herbs.</i>

07:45.850 --> 07:49.380
<i>Because I thought I'd need 
those to become an adventurer.</i>

07:50.190 --> 07:52.790
<i>So this exam will be easy for me.</i>

07:53.310 --> 07:55.230
<i>It's my second time taking it, too.</i>

07:59.320 --> 08:02.900
Sheesh, why was it so hard?

08:00.270 --> 08:02.290
Don't let it get you down.

08:02.290 --> 08:04.430
You're amazing, Rentt.

08:04.430 --> 08:06.230
I heard you got a perfect score.

08:06.230 --> 08:07.930
That's extremely rare.

08:07.930 --> 08:10.240
I'm just glad I passed.

08:10.240 --> 08:12.750
What will I be doing in the practical?

08:12.750 --> 08:17.170
You'll form a party with a few of the 
others and carry out a job for the guild.

08:17.650 --> 08:20.630
A job for the guild, huh?

08:21.290 --> 08:23.210
Ryze! Laura!

08:26.310 --> 08:30.410
You three will be forming a party today.

08:36.160 --> 08:38.130
I'm Ryze Danner, a swordsman.

08:38.680 --> 08:41.150
I use spirit energy to raise 
my strength when I fight.

08:41.150 --> 08:42.740
Let me fight in front.

08:43.040 --> 08:44.610
I'm Laura Sati.

08:44.610 --> 08:47.650
I'm a mage, and I can use healing magic.

08:47.650 --> 08:49.480
I'll do my best at the rear.

08:49.480 --> 08:50.960
Nice to meet you.

08:51.490 --> 08:53.140
I'm Rentt Vivie.

08:53.140 --> 08:54.430
Nice to meet you.

08:54.850 --> 08:58.210
I fight with a sword, too. I can 
use magic and spirit power.

08:58.900 --> 09:00.980
Okay, listen up, everyone!

09:01.330 --> 09:05.680
The practical exam involves completing 
a job prepared by the guild.

09:06.020 --> 09:08.070
It will take place at the 
Labyrinth of the New Moon.

09:08.070 --> 09:10.660
I will now hand out maps.

09:10.660 --> 09:14.710
Your job is to reach the 
point written on your map.

09:15.620 --> 09:18.270
What, so we just have to get here?

09:18.690 --> 09:20.650
You have until sunset!

09:20.950 --> 09:22.210
Dismissed!

09:22.210 --> 09:25.460
Um, are there any restrictions?

09:25.460 --> 09:26.920
None in particular.

09:26.920 --> 09:28.890
You can do anything you like.

09:28.890 --> 09:31.520
Are we all headed for the same spot?

09:31.520 --> 09:34.540
Yes. You're all going to a single location.

09:34.820 --> 09:40.410
The first party to arrive will receive 
a reward befitting their efforts.

09:41.690 --> 09:44.590
So it's a race, huh?

09:45.090 --> 09:46.970
It's a race...

09:47.610 --> 09:48.550
Yeah.

10:02.300 --> 10:06.500
Rentt, you ever been to the 
Labyrinth of the New Moon?

10:06.500 --> 10:07.580
Yeah.

10:07.580 --> 10:09.820
I see. Me too.

10:09.820 --> 10:11.920
Just partway through 
the first floor, though.

10:13.030 --> 10:14.510
That still counts.

10:14.510 --> 10:17.920
I'll be Bronze-class soon, and 
then I'll go further down.

10:17.920 --> 10:19.520
Let's hurry.

10:19.520 --> 10:20.220
Yeah.

10:20.220 --> 10:21.190
Wait.

10:22.140 --> 10:23.730
What do you want, Rentt?

10:23.730 --> 10:25.710
We should buy a map.

10:26.820 --> 10:29.610
We can't use the map we were given?

10:30.220 --> 10:33.870
This map is 15 years old.

10:34.720 --> 10:38.450
This old map won't be very reliable.

10:38.450 --> 10:40.750
Damn it! They tried to trick us!

10:41.270 --> 10:43.660
Hey! Rentt?

10:46.570 --> 10:48.800
Can I help you?

10:50.360 --> 10:52.090
I'd like to buy a map.

10:52.090 --> 10:56.310
A map. Of course. That'll be two silvers.

10:56.310 --> 10:57.390
That's expensive!

10:57.390 --> 10:58.790
We can't afford that.

10:58.790 --> 11:00.640
We just need one for the first floor.

11:01.200 --> 11:04.140
That shouldn't cost more 
than five bronze pieces.

11:05.640 --> 11:07.360
You've got a deal.

11:07.670 --> 11:10.430
No fooling you, huh, sir?

11:11.040 --> 11:12.360
Sorry.

11:12.360 --> 11:15.200
Is that map really right?

11:15.810 --> 11:18.210
Compare it to the one you got.

11:18.760 --> 11:20.200
Um...

11:21.290 --> 11:23.220
This part had a cave-in?

11:23.220 --> 11:25.400
The path changed at this part, too!

11:25.670 --> 11:30.670
And look! This map has the 
location of all the traps, too!

11:30.670 --> 11:32.670
We won't get lost now!

11:32.670 --> 11:33.800
Yeah!

11:33.800 --> 11:37.810
If you want to pass, 
kiddos, do what he says.

11:41.250 --> 11:43.440
Not bad, Rentt.

11:43.440 --> 11:47.260
But why would the guild give us bad maps?

11:47.930 --> 11:54.320
Those carriages could've just as 
easily taken us to the wrong place.

11:57.340 --> 11:59.700
An adventurer can never 
let their guard down.

12:00.100 --> 12:04.090
The point of this exam is to see if you've 
got what it takes to be an adventurer.

12:04.090 --> 12:05.320
I see.

12:05.320 --> 12:08.200
Seriously? What a pain.

12:08.200 --> 12:09.540
Remember this.

12:09.540 --> 12:11.040
Remember what?

12:11.730 --> 12:15.130
The guild can be surprisingly mean.

12:36.110 --> 12:38.570
Don't let your guard down because 
they're just skeletons.

12:38.570 --> 12:40.140
I know that!

12:42.620 --> 12:43.980
Thanks, Laura!

12:43.980 --> 12:44.620
Sure!

12:56.200 --> 13:00.170
<i>They're pretty good for their age.</i>

13:00.170 --> 13:02.450
<i>They're working together as a team,</i>

13:02.450 --> 13:05.590
<i>and they've each got well-defined roles so 
that neither's doing too much for the other.</i>

13:10.890 --> 13:12.860
Are you both okay?

13:14.880 --> 13:18.310
Don't worry about me... 
is what I'd like to say.

13:18.870 --> 13:22.400
Were there always this many 
monsters around here?

13:25.690 --> 13:26.810
Rentt?

13:27.230 --> 13:29.690
The monsters are being lured here.

13:29.690 --> 13:31.290
Is that possible?

13:31.290 --> 13:34.320
Yeah. You use things like this.

13:35.780 --> 13:37.800
Incense?

13:40.220 --> 13:42.780
What's this doing here?

13:42.780 --> 13:44.290
You'll know soon.

13:45.030 --> 13:48.670
Also, there's an ambush up ahead.

13:49.590 --> 13:53.060
But none of the monsters here should 
have that level of intelligence.

13:53.060 --> 13:54.400
Not monsters.

13:56.040 --> 13:57.030
Don't tell me...

13:57.410 --> 14:01.150
That's right. The ones laying 
the ambush are human.

14:01.860 --> 14:03.550
But...

14:03.550 --> 14:06.260
We have to fight humans?

14:06.830 --> 14:08.380
Get ready.

14:09.680 --> 14:11.320
I'll take the lead.

14:25.370 --> 14:27.310
Watch out! There are two more!

14:28.920 --> 14:30.680
I told you, I'll take the front!

14:31.380 --> 14:32.540
That's right!

14:32.540 --> 14:33.850
I'll let you handle him, then.

14:34.440 --> 14:35.570
Right.

14:38.760 --> 14:40.150
<i>Wow...</i>

15:01.410 --> 15:02.440
Ryze!

15:06.050 --> 15:08.130
Thanks, Laura!

15:08.130 --> 15:09.590
Damn it! I can't see!

15:09.920 --> 15:12.190
This is payback!

15:13.990 --> 15:16.970
<i>Looks like they don't need my help.</i>

15:20.050 --> 15:20.810
Ryze!

15:22.020 --> 15:22.850
Yeah!

15:30.330 --> 15:32.250
W-We got 'em.

15:32.250 --> 15:33.780
It worked!

15:40.610 --> 15:44.180
They're taking the exam too, aren't they?

15:44.180 --> 15:45.720
Why would they do this?

15:45.720 --> 15:48.330
They wanted to make us fail the exam.

15:48.600 --> 15:51.730
The examiner did say you could do anything.

15:51.730 --> 15:53.020
Right, Rentt?

15:53.360 --> 15:56.380
Anything can happen in the Labyrinth.

15:56.380 --> 15:58.700
The monsters aren't the only threat.

15:59.180 --> 16:00.850
Now you understand, right?

16:01.130 --> 16:03.510
An adventurer can never 
let their guard down.

16:06.430 --> 16:07.480
Rentt.

16:09.690 --> 16:12.130
From now on, we'll obey your orders.

16:13.120 --> 16:14.350
Ryze.

16:16.730 --> 16:18.830
Let's keep an eye out as we move on.

16:19.230 --> 16:20.190
Right.

16:24.880 --> 16:26.790
Come pick them up quickly.

16:37.530 --> 16:38.900
He saw me?

16:38.900 --> 16:42.020
Hey, untie me, please.

16:42.020 --> 16:43.860
Oh, sorry.

16:45.120 --> 16:50.600
The man in the mask seemed to 
know you were sent by the guild.

16:50.600 --> 16:51.670
Seriously?

16:51.670 --> 16:52.950
Who is he?

16:52.950 --> 16:53.960
I don't know.

16:54.290 --> 16:57.590
Though I can think of one 
person it might be...

16:59.280 --> 17:01.800
Maybe my sister was right.

17:07.550 --> 17:10.470
Is there something I can 
do for you, Guildmaster?

17:10.820 --> 17:15.750
Relax. Being all formal in front 
of me won't earn you a raise.

17:15.750 --> 17:17.650
Yes, I know that.

17:19.180 --> 17:22.260
I heard a strange rumor about the incident.

17:23.550 --> 17:25.390
Rentt Vivie.

17:26.230 --> 17:29.040
The new adventurer you're in charge of.

17:29.510 --> 17:31.150
Has he done something wrong?

17:31.150 --> 17:34.440
Some people are saying he's the criminal.

17:35.910 --> 17:39.820
He showed up out of nowhere 
in Maalt. He's quite skilled.

17:39.820 --> 17:42.340
And we don't know anything about his past.

17:42.870 --> 17:45.700
If you want to say that's 
suspicious, I agree with you.

17:46.000 --> 17:49.240
But every adventurer has 
something in their past.

17:49.810 --> 17:52.320
That doesn't mean we can just 
ignore the accusation, however.

17:53.380 --> 17:57.380
If you learn anything, 
tell me immediately. Got it?

17:58.770 --> 17:59.730
Yes, sir.

18:07.070 --> 18:09.170
Our destination's just up ahead.

18:10.190 --> 18:14.070
This door... it's what I think it is, right?

18:14.070 --> 18:15.180
Yes.

18:15.180 --> 18:18.920
It's one of several boss 
rooms on this floor.

18:19.710 --> 18:23.290
There's no way to get to our destination 
except by going through it.

18:25.180 --> 18:27.150
You ever fought a boss?

18:27.530 --> 18:28.860
Not yet.

18:28.860 --> 18:31.180
It's not something two 
Iron-classes can handle.

18:31.180 --> 18:32.320
Scared?

18:32.900 --> 18:34.800
Of course not!

18:36.430 --> 18:41.020
There's no shame for an adventurer 
in avoiding a fight you can't win.

18:44.290 --> 18:48.310
What, we're not the first?

18:48.890 --> 18:51.260
They think they can beat 
us to the goal, huh?

18:51.610 --> 18:53.610
Other examinees?

18:53.610 --> 18:54.470
Good timing.

18:55.000 --> 18:56.330
Good timing?

18:57.100 --> 19:01.420
A party with two kids and 
a weirdo in a mask. Great.

19:03.060 --> 19:05.120
We're both taking the same exam.

19:05.120 --> 19:07.330
I don't appreciate being talked to that way.

19:07.680 --> 19:09.570
What, you're lecturing us?

19:09.570 --> 19:11.320
Who do you think you are?

19:11.320 --> 19:14.540
Hey, that girl's actually pretty cute.

19:15.000 --> 19:17.500
Hey, want to come with us instead?

19:18.650 --> 19:20.210
Don't you dare speak to Laura.

19:20.210 --> 19:22.300
Who are you, kid?

19:22.300 --> 19:24.130
We got here first.

19:24.130 --> 19:25.120
Don't get in our way.

19:25.120 --> 19:26.250
What?

19:27.870 --> 19:30.970
H-Hey, it was a joke!

19:30.970 --> 19:35.270
I'm sorry. I don't have 
much of a sense of humor.

19:35.270 --> 19:37.240
Look, I'm sorry!

19:37.240 --> 19:39.000
We're not going to try to stop 
you from going in first.

19:39.000 --> 19:39.580
Right?

19:39.580 --> 19:40.700
Y-Yeah!

19:41.820 --> 19:43.370
You can go in first.

19:44.290 --> 19:46.420
We're going to rest a little, first.

19:47.230 --> 19:50.180
Okay, we'll take you up on that.

19:50.180 --> 19:51.020
R-Right.

19:51.370 --> 19:52.260
Thanks!

19:58.410 --> 20:01.520
We're lucky they were so dumb!

20:03.310 --> 20:05.430
What are you doing, Rentt?

20:05.430 --> 20:07.750
If they beat us there, we lose!

20:07.750 --> 20:08.640
Why?

20:08.640 --> 20:11.190
Why? It's a race, isn't it?

20:12.100 --> 20:15.570
I'm sure Rentt has a reason, don't you?

20:15.570 --> 20:17.250
So you figured it out, Laura?

20:20.210 --> 20:23.440
You wanted to show us what a 
boss fight looks like, first?

20:23.440 --> 20:26.670
That's part of it. But not all.

20:27.290 --> 20:29.920
My leg! My leg!

20:39.900 --> 20:43.440
Those were guild employees, weren't they?

20:43.440 --> 20:46.170
Yes. Even if you lose, you won't die.

20:47.630 --> 20:49.060
Feel better?

20:50.900 --> 20:52.180
Well...

20:52.510 --> 20:54.610
Like I said.

20:54.610 --> 20:58.230
There's no shame for an adventurer 
in avoiding a fight you can't win.

21:00.780 --> 21:02.600
Maybe you're right.

21:02.600 --> 21:05.570
But no, that's not what I meant!

21:06.060 --> 21:10.530
If I run away here, I don't 
think I'll ever come back.

21:11.610 --> 21:14.400
I'll never be a real adventurer.

21:16.110 --> 21:17.270
Ryze...

21:18.120 --> 21:21.970
So... will you come with me, Laura?

21:23.300 --> 21:24.220
Yeah.

21:25.380 --> 21:27.510
You've made your decision, then.

21:28.920 --> 21:31.750
<i>An adventurer who's been 
broken once becomes weak.</i>

21:32.340 --> 21:38.880
<i>Once that happens, it's not rare at all for 
adventurers to just quit the job entirely.</i>

21:39.530 --> 21:45.070
